first can you just say and spell your  first and last name for me  my name is dr amy stone a-m-y-s-t-o-n-e  great and then your title position and  where you work  i'm an assistant professor of  microbiology and immunology at toro  university nevada  great so we're here to talk a little bit  about this cova 19 study that you guys  are doing and also looking for  volunteers so  first just kind of break down what  exactly the goal of this study is and  what you hope to accomplish  the goal of our study is to understand  how the las vegas metro area and clark  county as a whole  have been affected by  the virus  that causes covet 19 immunologically so  we're looking at antibodies and so we  want to understand how  how are the antibodies being produced by  our community and so what that tells us  is it tells us a little bit about  protection it tells us about who has  been infected and it tells us about who  is getting vaccinated all of this  information can help us understand where  we need to put our resources as the  public health efforts and lead to  hopefully  new treatments and vaccines that will  help prevent and treat this disease  and if you can kind of break it down  maybe in layman's terms in terms of once  you collect this blood sample how  exactly you go about figuring out that  information that you're looking for yeah  after we collect the blood we bring it  into the lab and we separate it into a  couple different sections so first we  take out the liquid and within the  liquid are the proteins which is also  where the antibodies are so that's where  we're going to find  those  molecules that are going to help protect  us against the virus  we also are looking at white blood cells  we want to know how the white blood  cells are able to function in people who  have been vaccinated versus have not  been vaccinated people who have had the  disease versus people who haven't had  the disease and what we're hoping to  find by looking at these white blood  cells is if there's any indication to  how we might predict if someone is going  to have severe disease or mild disease  and so  it sounds like you're looking to get  these samples from both folks who are  unvaccinated and vaccinated correct  yes we are looking to get samples from  people who are vaccinated and  unvaccinated people who have been  infected and people who haven't been  infected we really need to look at  everyone to get a clear picture of  what's happening in our community and so  we can't  exclude any one of those groups because  they are representative of our community  and uh if you can kind of  explain the  how it works when you look at these  antibodies and you uh  try to decide the efficacy of the  vaccines what exactly are you looking  for to make that determination  so when we take the antibodies what  we're going to be doing is  seeing how well they attach to the virus  so we have pieces of the virus that are  being targeted by these antibodies so  the virus is kind of like a ball we've  all seen that image and the parts that  are sticking out of the ball that's  called the spike protein  we want our antibodies to bind to that  spike protein because that's what what's  going to stop those viruses from  attacking us and infecting us  and so we want to know how  well do those antibodies from our  community attach to that spike protein  and does that actually stop the virus  from getting into  someone's cells  what do you mention  i'm not trying to answer that fully  tonight no you're fine  um and  earlier you talked about you know  gathering the information from this  study and then determining where best to  put resources so what exactly are those  resources that you're talking about  we've partnered with the southern nevada  public health district to share our data  we're looking at zip codes and where  people who report either being  vaccinated or being infected from this  information by zip code we can look at  where some where there might be hot  spots of infection and then the public  health district can send out the  interventions that we need and make sure  that people are  being protected and making sure that  those areas have the  clinical workers the healthcare workers  they need in order to support their  community and maintain the health of  their community  i know currently you know within the  clark county area we have you know those  current zip code maps right that show  like you said hot spots for covet  infection and then areas that are maybe  are more vaccinated than others uh is  this  you know looking at the antibodies  specifically is this maybe more of a  accurate indication is that kind of your  your hope when you when you do get this  data to kind of supplement those  existing tools that we have  our data will supplement the existing  tools that we have that currently show  hot spots because our data will be able  to show the asymptomatic infections when  you are surveilling a community  typically you're only looking at people  who come to the clinic with symptoms our  group is looking at everyone whether  they've had symptoms or not and so we'll  be able to identify people who had no  symptoms that have been affected with  the virus and that will give us a much  better picture of the real level of  transmission as opposed to just the  level of transmission that leads to  clinical disease  that makes sense uh and i know you're  obviously looking for volunteers  um i guess around how many volunteers is  is ideal and do you think  you know if you reach that number will  that be inaccurate representation of  of that population that you're looking  at  we think that around a thousand  participants will be an accurate  representation of the las vegas metro  area um we would always love to have  more more data is always better  and so what we're looking for are just  any individual who is an adult  over 110 pounds so that they can safely  donate blood  um to come out and give us a small  sample of blood  and if we can get a thousand people we  think that will be a really good  representation of our community  i see that you know the goal is to you  know publish findings uh next year um i  know you talk about obviously the the  goal of this is to  figure out where to where to put the  resources how important  is a study like this can you kind of  speak to just the importance of doing  something like this  our type of study is incredibly  important for our community there are  similar studies going on all over the  world however what's happening in other  cities such as seattle new york or l.a  doesn't really represent what's  happening here in las vegas and so we  need this study from our local community  to understand our local needs  great and um obviously you're looking  for people over 18 you mentioned  weighing at least 110 pounds um how how  do people get in touch with you guys to  be a part of this study we're asking  people who are interested in our study  to send us an email  at  t u n  covid 19 study and that's all one word  at gmail.com that's our study gmail  after people contact us we reply with  more information and if they're still  interested we schedule them for the  blood draw we're doing  appointments only and those are going to  be at the southern nevada public health  district maine clinic  that's sort of in the middle of the city  on decatur  is there anything else that you wanted  to add  i'm  yeah  our study is particularly important in  this moment because of the rise in cases  that we've seen here in august and the  rise of the delta variant what we don't  know from a lot of the vaccines is how  long will protection last and how good  is that protection against the delta  variant  our information from this study will be  able to give some of that information  we'll be able to test  individuals antibodies against  the delta variant and see are they  protected or are they not and whether  natural vaccine  natural infection vaccination or  vaccination vaccination after natural  infection will result in good protection  what we really want is to understand how  do we protect our community and there  are so many open questions that really  need answered  great well thank you very much for your  time i really appreciated chatting with  you  thank you so much for giving us the  opportunity to talk about it and share  the information
 

